## Why This Is Asked

This question tests the ability to design cross-modal, real-time computer vision pipelines that integrate on-device adaptation with differentiable geometry for robotic manipulation and planning in unstructured environments.

## Key Concepts

- Real-time monocular depth and surface normals estimation from a single RGB camera
- Differentiable probabilistic mesh prediction integrated with motion planning
- Few-shot (5-shot) on-device adaptation using synthetic pre-training followed by real-world fine-tuning
- Multi-task learning with shared encoders and task-specific heads

## Code Example

```javascript
// Core inference pipeline sketch
function forwardPass(frame) {
  const features = sharedEncoder(frame);
  const depth = depthHead(features);
  const normals = normalHead(features);
  const mesh = meshHead(features);
  return { depth, normals, mesh };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you quantify uncertainty in the mesh predictions to ensure safe manipulation?
- What strategies would you use to handle reflective or texture-less surfaces where depth estimation typically fails?
- How does the system handle dynamic scene changes between adaptation and deployment?

## Why This Is Asked

This question probes on-device real-time hazard detection and 3D distance estimation under unseen categories, reflecting safety-critical constraints common in field deployments.

## Key Concepts

- Real-time monocular depth on edge
- On-device meta-learning (5-shot)
- Synthetic+real data with domain randomization
- Temporal tracking and occlusion robustness
- Evaluation: detection, depth error, latency

## Code Example

```javascript
function forward(img, backbone, detectorHead, depthHead) {
  const feats = backbone.extract(img);
  const boxes = detectorHead.predict(feats);
  const depth = depthHead.predict(feats);
  return { boxes, depth };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you ablate depth head accuracy vs. detector latency?
- What failure modes dominate in cluttered sites, and how would you mitigate them?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a complete edge-CV pipeline: real-time monocular 3D pose with per-object velocity, occlusion robustness, and rapid on-device adaptation to unseen parts. Emphasizes practical data strategies and evaluation in an industrial setting.

## Key Concepts
- Real-time monocular 3D pose estimation
- Per-instance velocity prediction for planning
- On-device few-shot adaptation (5-shot)
- Occlusion handling and data fusion strategies

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: forward pass with adaptation trigger
function forward(frame, exemplars){
  let features = backbone(frame);
  let detections = detector(features);
  let poses = poseHead(features, detections);
  let vel = velocityHead(features, detections, previous);
  if (exemplars) adapt(poses, exemplars);
  return {detections, poses, vel};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you quantify robustness to occlusion in your evaluation?
- What ablation would you run to isolate the velocity head contribution?

## Why This Question Is Asked

This question evaluates the ability to design a real-time monocular system integrating segmentation, 3D pose estimation with scene priors, grasp-point planning, and physics-based stability reasoning—plus efficient edge adaptation with minimal shots.

## Key Concepts

- Monocular 3D pose estimation using environmental priors
- Grasp-point prediction in cluttered scenes
- Differentiable physics modules for stability evaluation
- On-device few-shot adaptation strategies

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode outline for the model heads
function forward(img, shelfPrior) {
  const features = backbone(img);
  const segmentation = segmentationHead(features);
  const pose = poseHead(features, shelfPrior);
  const grasp = graspHead(features, pose);
  const stability = physicsPrior(grasp, pose);
  return { segmentation, pose, grasp, stability };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a practical monocular 6-DoF pose estimator that handles symmetry, occlusion, and online adaptation in a real-world manufacturing setting. Emphasizes differentiable refinement, data strategies, and latency planning.

## Key Concepts
- Monocular 6-DoF pose estimation
- Differentiable rendering for pose refinement
- Symmetry handling and occlusion robustness
- Synthetic data + domain randomization
- Online adaptation with few-shot updates
- Real-time latency targets (embedded GPU)

## Code Example
```javascript
class PoseHead {
  constructor(featDim) {
    this.fcRot = linear(featDim, 4); // quaternion
    this.fcTrans = linear(featDim, 3);
  }
  forward(feat) {
    const q = normalize(this.fcRot(feat), 2);
    const t = this.fcTrans(feat);
    return { quat: q, trans: t };
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate symmetry handling for objects with known symmetry? 
- How would you mitigate catastrophic forgetting during online adaptation?

